course: dictionary
lesson: 7656
title: Promptly: quick, on time, or straight after
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Promptly is a word that tells you how or when something happens. It can mean quickly, without waiting, or exactly on time. To find the right meaning, read the words around it.
explain: «Please arrive promptly at 9 o'clock.» Here the clue is the time, so promptly means exactly on time. You must not be late.
explain: Promptly can also mean right after something else, often with a funny result. «He sat down and promptly fell asleep.» He fell asleep straight after he sat down. The word shows that one thing happened at once after the other.
explain: In a story, «Mole promptly had another fit of the blues» means his sad feeling came straight away, with no pause. To check, swap in quickly or right away. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Promptly is an adverb: it tells you how or when an action happens.
fact: «Promptly» means quickly, without waiting.
fact: «Promptly» can mean exactly on time, as in «at 9 o'clock promptly».
fact: «Promptly» can mean right after something else, often with a funny result.
fact: Useful phrases: promptly at, and reply promptly.
exercise: «Please arrive promptly at 9 o'clock.» What does promptly mean here? | Long after the bell | *Exactly on time | Somewhere else | Slowly and quietly
exercise: «He sat down and promptly fell asleep.» What does promptly show? | He never sat down at all | He fell asleep the next day | *He fell asleep straight after sitting down | He sat down very slowly
exercise: In «Mole promptly had another fit of the blues», what does promptly mean? | *Straight away, right after something else | Very quietly | Not at all | Slowly, with a long pause
test: «Please reply promptly to the letter.» What does reply promptly mean? | *Reply quickly, without waiting | Write a very long letter | Reply next year | Do not reply at all
test: The bus starts promptly at 8 o'clock. What does promptly tell you? | It starts late, whenever it is ready | *It starts exactly on time | It may start early or late, it does not matter | It starts slowly
exam: «She promptly apologised when she spilled the juice.» Which meaning fits? | Very slowly and carefully | *Straight away, right after the spill | Not at all | Exactly at 9 o'clock
